 # Recoverable dependency scheduler
 
-Implementation and self-test documentation goes here.
+`scheduler.cjs` exports `createScheduler({ file, concurrency, execute, onStage })`.
+It returns `enqueue(jobs)`, `run()`, and `snapshot()`. Jobs use lowercase IDs matching
+`^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$`; dependencies can refer to jobs in the same batch or to
+previously enqueued jobs. `run()` executes ready jobs in ID order, bounded by the
+configured concurrency, and persists a JSON checkpoint after every accepted enqueue,
+claim, and terminal transition.
+
+Run the self-tests with:
+
+```sh
+node --test test.cjs
+```
+
+Recovery is at-least-once: a process interruption after a durable claim can replay
+the side effect with a higher attempt number. A completed result is durable before
+the completed stage callback, so completed work is not replayed after restart.
+The checkpoint is atomically replaced through a temporary file and stale temporary
+files are ignored.
